course: dictionary
lesson: 13691
title: Innovation: new ideas that change things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An innovation is a new idea, invention or way of doing something. The word comes from innovate, which means to make changes or bring in something new. «The new bike lock was a clever innovation that stopped thieves.» Clever and new tell you the lock is an invention, so innovation means a new invention here.
explain: Innovation can also mean a better way of doing things, not only a gadget. «Our class found a faster way to sort the recycling, and the teacher called it a useful innovation.» Nothing was built here, but the change is new and helpful, so it counts as an innovation.
explain: Look for clue words around the word: new, idea, invention, change, better, clever. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check. «The school's design-and-make challenge produced a clever innovation» still makes sense if you say «a clever new invention».
fact: Innovation means making new ideas, methods or inventions, or making changes to how things are done.
fact: An innovation is a new idea, invention or way of doing something.
fact: «Innovation» is a noun, and its plural is «innovations».
fact: Famous innovations include the printing press, the steam engine, vaccines and the internet.
fact: Useful phrases are «technological innovation» and «a major innovation».
exercise: «The class's solar lamp was a clever innovation.» What is an innovation here? | A school trip | A kind of sunshine | *A new idea or invention | A broken lamp
exercise: Innovation can mean changing how things are done. Which is an example? | Sleeping in on a Sunday | Sitting in the same seat every day | *A new, faster way to sort the recycling | Forgetting to bring a pencil
exercise: Find and copy the plural form of innovation. | innovates | *innovations | innovation
test: What is a major innovation? | A small, broken toy | A type of cold weather | A school rule that never changes | *A big, important new idea or invention
test: Which of these is an example of technological innovation? | *The steam engine | A bedtime story | A lost sock | A sunny afternoon
exam: «The school's design-and-make challenge produced a clever innovation: a bag that charges a phone.» What does innovation mean here? | A school holiday | A kind of packed lunch | *A new invention or idea | A music lesson
